Article 34

1. Efforts to prevent violence against women and children are carried out in an integrated manner by the Regional Government and coordinated by the technical Regional Apparatus.
2. Prevention efforts as referred to in paragraph (1) are implemented by:
a. conducting guidance towards harmonious household integrity;
b. forming a network in efforts to prevent violence;
c. conducting coordination, integration, and synchronization of violence prevention based on partnership patterns;
d. establishing a violence prevention system;
e. conducting socialization regarding laws and regulations related to the protection of women and children victims of violence; and
f. providing critical education regarding the rights of women and children for the community.

Article 44

1. The Regional Government, in organizing the protection of women and children from acts of violence, establishes P2TP2A as a regional technical service implementing unit (UPTDD) integrated into the Technical Regional Apparatus.
2. The organization of protection and services for women and children victims of violence is carried out in an integrated manner by P2TP2A.
3. The organization of services for women and children victims of violence as referred to in paragraph (1) includes:
a. providing fast and free services to victims;
b. organizing protection and fulfillment of victims' rights to health rehabilitation, social rehabilitation, return, social reintegration, and legal assistance;
c. cooperating with certain institutions in providing translators and volunteer assistants needed for victims;
d. networking with government or private hospitals for treatment and health recovery of victims and cooperating with witness and victim protection institutions, social shelters, or trauma centers owned by the government, community, or other institutions for health recovery of victims;
e. providing convenience, comfort, and safety for victims;
f. maintaining the confidentiality of victims; and
g. providing fulfillment of legal assistance for victims.
4. Further provisions regarding the establishment, procedures, and mechanisms for organizing P2TP2A are regulated by Regent Regulation.

