CHAPTER V

RIGHTS OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE

Article 45

Every woman and child victim of violence receives the following rights:

a. right to complaint handling;
b. right to have their dignity respected as human beings;
c. right to receive protection from family, community, regional government and/or other parties either temporarily or based on court protection orders;
d. right to health and psychological recovery from the suffering experienced by victims;
e. right to determine their own decisions;
f. right to special handling related to victim confidentiality;
g. right to obtain information;
h. right to confidentiality of identity;
i. right to social rehabilitation;
j. right to assistance by social workers and legal aid at every level of the examination process in accordance with laws and regulations; and
k. right to spiritual guidance services.

Article 34

1. Efforts to prevent violence against women and children are carried out in an integrated manner by the Regional Government and coordinated by the technical Regional Apparatus.
2. Prevention efforts as referred to in paragraph (1) are implemented by:
a. conducting guidance towards harmonious household integrity;
b. forming a network in efforts to prevent violence;
c. conducting coordination, integration, and synchronization of violence prevention based on partnership patterns;
d. establishing a violence prevention system;
e. conducting socialization regarding laws and regulations related to the protection of women and children victims of violence; and
f. providing critical education regarding the rights of women and children for the community.

Article 44

1. The Regional Government, in organizing the protection of women and children from acts of violence, establishes P2TP2A as a regional technical service implementing unit (UPTDD) integrated into the Technical Regional Apparatus.
2. The organization of protection and services for women and children victims of violence is carried out in an integrated manner by P2TP2A.
3. The organization of services for women and children victims of violence as referred to in paragraph (1) includes:
a. providing fast and free services to victims;
b. organizing protection and fulfillment of victims' rights to health rehabilitation, social rehabilitation, return, social reintegration, and legal assistance;
c. cooperating with certain institutions in providing translators and volunteer assistants needed for victims;
d. networking with government or private hospitals for treatment and health recovery of victims and cooperating with witness and victim protection institutions, social shelters, or trauma centers owned by the government, community, or other institutions for health recovery of victims;
e. providing convenience, comfort, and safety for victims;
f. maintaining the confidentiality of victims; and
g. providing fulfillment of legal assistance for victims.
4. Further provisions regarding the establishment, procedures, and mechanisms for organizing P2TP2A are regulated by Regent Regulation.

Article 4

Every Woman has the right:

a. to life and the right to maintain life and livelihood;
b. to form a family and continue offspring through lawful marriage;
c. to develop themselves through the fulfillment of their basic needs;
d. to obtain education and benefit from science and technology, arts and culture, in order to improve the quality of life and for the welfare of mankind;
e. to advance themselves in fighting for their rights collectively to build society, nation and state;
f. to recognition, guarantee, protection and fair legal certainty as well as equal treatment before the law;
g. to work and receive fair and proper remuneration and treatment in employment relations;
h. to obtain equal opportunities in government;
i. to freedom of association, assembly and expression of opinion;
j. to protection of self, family, honor, dignity and property under their control, and the right to a sense of security and protection from threats of fear to do or not do something that is a basic right;
k. to be free from torture or treatment that degrades human dignity and the right to obtain political asylum from other countries;
l. to live in prosperity physically and mentally, to reside and obtain a good and healthy living environment, and the right to obtain health services;
m. to social security that enables their development fully as dignified human beings;
n. to equality of their position in law and government; to decent work and livelihood for humanity;
o. in the defense of the state;
p. to communicate and obtain information to develop their personal and social environment, and the right to seek, obtain, possess, store, process, and convey information using all types of available channels;
q. to embrace their respective religions and to worship according to their religion and beliefs; and
r. to obtain education.

Article 3

This Regional Regulation aims to:

a. guarantee the fulfillment of the rights of women and children;
b. maintain the integrity of the household in order to realize a harmonious family;
c. prevent violence against women and children;
d. protect and provide a sense of security for women and children;
e. provide services to women and children victims of acts of violence;
f. provide protection to reporters and witnesses; and
g. carry out empowerment for women victims of violence.

